<title>JAPAN: Japan June pork imports fall 87.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June pork imports fall 87.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in June totalled 17,982 tonnes, down 87.6 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>The details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     June 97	May 97	 June 96</p>
<p> Total	     17,982	 34,285	 145,523</p>
<p> Refrigerated     8,671	 13,484	  16,312</p>
<p> Frozen	     9,311	 20,801	 129,211</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan		 nil	    nil	   8,374</p>
<p> U.S.		 6,555	 10,327	   6,831</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     June 97	May 97	  June 96</p>
<p> Taiwan		 164	   31	    37,350</p>
<p> U.S.		 1,908	  3,850	  19,045</p>
<p> Denmark	    2,631	  7,729	  44,380</p>
<p> Canada	     1,185	  3,394	   7,313</p>
<p> U.K.		   237	    796	   2,173</p>
<p>Total imports of refrigerated pork in the first six months of this year totalled 62,604 tonnes, against 85,076 tonnes in the same period of last year.</p>
<p>Total imports of frozen pork in the January-June period of this year totalled 108,706 tonnes, against 353,891 tonnes a year earlier, ministry data showed.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
